    "body": "On Ascend NPUs, ZeRO++ quantized weights and gradients carry twice the quantization error of CUDA, biased toward zero, and int4 qgZ gradients come back about a third too small.\n\n`NPUQuantizer._quantize_groups` truncates `x * scale`. The CUDA kernel rounds half to even (`__float2int_rn`, before the `(int8_t)` cast), and `test_quantize.py` checks it against `torch.round`.\n\nFix: `trunc_()` to `round_()`, plus the docstring. The new CPU test, at the path the docstring already cites, checks int8 `quantize` and int4 `swizzle_quant` against that reference. It fails on master and passes here.\n\nBefore to after, on CPU:\n- int8: L1 error 1.99x to 1.00x the reference, mean error -0.50 to 0.00 steps\n- int4 qgZ sum (2 nodes x 2 devices) as a fraction of the exact sum: 0.67 to 1.00\n- upstream `test_float_quantize` (int8 symmetric) on `NPUQuantizer`: 30 of 60 fail, then all pass\n\nVerified on Ascend 910B4 by @VenusTZZ: qgZ int4 mean reconstruction error 0.1198 to 0.0506.\n\n",
